  "sourceNotes": [
   {
    "id": 1,
    "text": "OCI statement shows (45,953,144); its own lines give (59,294,377) + 13,341,234 = (45,953,143). The equity statement uses (45,953,143).",
    "amount": 1
   },
   {
    "id": 2,
    "text": "Dividends declared 7,277,144,038 (equity statement) differ from dividends paid 7,277,190,123 (CF) by 46,085. Handled through a dividends-payable bridge.",
    "amount": 46085
   },
   {
    "id": 3,
    "text": "Note 3 accumulated depreciation at 31-Dec-2025 stated as 21,492,392,948; the roll-forward gives ...949. The balance-sheet net figure 38,192,488,081 agrees with ...949.",
    "amount": 1
   },
   {
    "id": 4,
    "text": "Note 3, computers: disposal at cost (1,214,605) vs accumulated depreciation released (1,214,606), a 1 EGP gap.",
    "amount": 1
   },
   {
    "id": 5,
    "text": "CF line \"Formed of expected credit losses on cash\" +10,382,262 is added to cash despite the word \"formed\". Taken as reported.",
    "amount": 10382262
   },
   {
    "id": 6,
    "text": "The CF labels customer advances \"(lease liability)\"; it is the contract liability. Label error in the source."
   },
   {
    "id": 7,
    "text": "Capex in the CF (5,848,069,006) equals Note 3 additions including PUC exactly. Other assets also moved, 68.2M to 79.6M."
   },
   {
    "id": 9,
    "text": "FY2025 statement of financial position, PDF page 5: the six non-current asset lines sum to 50,015,842,514, but the printed total is 50,015,842,515, and total assets 61,193,831,633. Confirmed in the PDF: this is in the source, not a transcription gap. The balance sheet ties within this documented 1 EGP.",
    "amount": 1
   },
   {
    "id": 10,
    "text": "Note 3, PDF page 13: at 31-Dec-2024, total cost 53,861,582,606 less accumulated depreciation 19,229,575,610 gives 34,632,006,996; the printed net, which the column sum and the balance sheet support, is 34,632,006,997.",
    "amount": 1
   },
   {
    "id": 11,
    "text": "Note 34, PDF page 29: shareholders dividends shown as 7,277,144,039; the equity statement shows 7,277,144,038.",
    "amount": 1
   },
   {
    "id": 12,
    "text": "Note 34, PDF page 29: the FY2024 column prints 6,927,357,966 after distributions, but the lines give 6,297,357,965, and neither produces the printed EPS of 5.27. EPS 5.27 = 15,119,739,368 / 2,868,140,263, with no distributions deducted.",
    "amount": 630000001
   },
   {
    "id": 13,
    "text": "FY2024 legal reserve transfer 478,114,534 is not 5% of reported FY2023 net profit 5,974,356,398 (298,717,820), because the FY2023 income statement excludes the merged company. The implied base is 9,562,290,680.",
    "amount": 179396714
   },
   {
    "id": 14,
    "text": "Merger: resolved by EGM 4-Nov-2023, approved by GAFI 21-Sep-2023, base date 31-Dec-2022, entered in the commercial register 13-Dec-2023 (Note 1). So FY2023 is mixed: the balance sheet is post-merger and the income statement is MOPCO before the merger. Not comparable with FY2024 and FY2025."
   },
   {
    "id": 15,
    "text": "FY2024 CF additions line 1,275,986,560 includes other assets (Note 3 additions 1,248,933,200). The FY2025 line equals Note 3 additions exactly (see note 7)."
   },
   {
    "id": 16,
    "text": "Employee distribution paid in 2025, 1,511,973,937, equals 10% of FY2024 net profit, not 10% of dividends. It exceeds salaries in cost of sales (858,088,584). Whether it breaches the Art. 41 wages cap needs total wages and the Arabic text. No cap is applied in the model.",
    "amount": 1511973937
   },
   {
    "id": 8,
    "text": "Debtors and other debit balances: BS change +603,590,502 does not match the CF line +113,856,513. Shown in the reconciliation table; the CF line is not derived from it."
   }
  ]
 },
